<!DOCTYPE html> 
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title>VM TRUCK ACADEMY - Push-Rod Inspection</title> 

  <!-- Animate on scroll (optional) -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/animate.css/4.1.1/animate.min.css"/>

  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f4f4f4;
      color: #333;
      transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 900px;
      background: #fff;
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
      animation: fadeIn 1s ease-in;
    }

    @keyframes fadeIn {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }
      to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 1.8em;
      color: #004080;
    }

    img {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      margin: 10px auto;
      display: block;
    }

    audio {
      width: 100%;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    ul {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
    }

    li {
      margin: 20px 0;
      background: #f9f9f9;
      padding: 15px;
      border-left: 4px solid #004080;
      border-radius: 6px;
      transition: background 0.3s ease;
    }

    li:hover {
      background: #e8f0ff;
    }

    li strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }

    i {
      color: #555;
    }

    a {
      color: #004080;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .download-btn {
      display: inline-block;
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 12px 20px;
      background-color: #004080;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
      border-radius: 6px;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: bold;
      transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
    }

    .download-btn:hover {
      background-color: #003366;
    }

    footer {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 0.9em;
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding: 20px;
      color: #666;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .container {
        padding: 15px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 1.5em;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <div class="container" id="pdfContent">
    <img src="image/vmlogo.png" alt="VM Truck Academy Logo" width="225" height="56">
    <h1 class="animate__animated animate__fadeInDown">Push-Rod Inspection Procedure</h1>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>1. Enter Cab</strong><i>"The wheels are chocked, both parking brakes are applied, My truck & trailer secure"</i><audio controls><source src="Incab01.mp3"></audio></li>

      <li><strong>2. Start Engine & Ask Examiner</strong>
        <br>– Release both parking brakes
        <br>– Pull hood latch
        <br>– Ask examiner which side to inspect
        <br>– Turn steering wheel accordingly
      </li>

      <li><strong>3. Turn Off Engine, Ignition ON (90–100 PSI)</strong>
        <i>"My current pressure is ____psi"</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push02.mp3"></audio>
      </li>

      <li><strong>4. Exit Truck & Open Hood</strong></li>

      <li><strong>5. Inspect Brake Chamber</strong>
        <i>"This brake chamber has a circular connection port..."</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push03.mp3"></audio>
        <br><img src="st.jpg" alt="Standard Stroke">
        <br><img src="ls.jpg" alt="Long Stroke">
        <br><img src="tag.jpg" alt="Plastic Tag">
      </li>

      <li><strong>6. Measure Brake Chamber Size & Adjustment Limit</strong>
        <i>"My Brake-chamber tool reads: 20 ... Adjustment limit is 1.75\""</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push04.mp3"></audio>
        <br><img src="braketool.jpg" alt="Brake Tool 1">
        <br><img src="braketool2.png" alt="Brake Tool 2">
        <br><img src="chart.jpg" alt="Adjustment Chart">
      </li>

      <li><strong>7. If Disc Brakes, Say:</strong>
        <i>"My truck has disc brakes, I will continue verbally."</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push05.mp3"></audio>
      </li>

      <li><strong>8. Mark the Push-Rod</strong>
        <i>"I will mark the push rod at the base of the brake chamber with chalk"</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push06.mp3"></audio>
        <br><img src="mark.jpg" alt="Mark Pushrod">
      </li>

      <li><strong>9. Re-Enter Truck & Apply Brake-Buddy</strong>
        <i>"I will fully apply my service brake with the brake buddy"</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push07.mp3"></audio>
        <br><img src="brakeb.jpg" alt="Brake Buddy">
      </li>

      <li><strong>10. Exit Truck & Measure Push-Rod Movement</strong>
        <i>"I will measure how far the mark moved from the base"</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push08.mp3"></audio>
        <br><img src="measure.jpg" alt="Measurement">
      </li>

      <li><strong>11. Read Push-Rod Measurement</strong>
        <i>"My push-rod moved 1\" ... within adjustment limit"</i>
        <audio controls><source src="Push09.mp3"></audio>
      </li>

      <li><strong>12. Remove Brake-Buddy & Apply Parking Brakes</strong></li>
      <li><strong>13. Read Minor & Major Defects</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <p>To see video of Push-Rod Inspection Procedure: 
      <a href="https://youtu.be/qrLOIjHTp7E?feature=shared" target="_blank">Press Here!</a>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="index.html">
        <img src="image/button_home.png" alt="Back to Home" style="width:156px;height:56px;">
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="download-btn" onclick="downloadPDF()">Download This Page as PDF</div>
  </div>

  <footer>
    © 2025 VM Truck Academy
  </footer>

  <!-- html2pdf.js library -->
  <script src="https://rawcdn.githack.com/eKoopmans/html2pdf/0.10.1/dist/html2pdf.bundle.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    function downloadPDF() {
      const element = document.getElementById('pdfContent');
      const opt = {
        margin: 0.5,
        filename: 'PushRodInspection_VMTruckAcademy.pdf',
        image: { type: 'jpeg', quality: 0.98 },
        html2canvas: { scale: 2 },
        jsPDF: { unit: 'in', format: 'letter', orientation: 'portrait' }
      };
      html2pdf().set(opt).from(element).save();
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>